Ladybird keeps a block-level input clear of floats, as it does any box
that establishes a block formatting context. The other engines do the
same for every form control. WebKit’s RenderBox::avoidsFloats() is true
for any form control element, and Blink’s LayoutTextControlSingleLine::
CreatesNewFormattingContext() returns true. Gecko’s text-control frame
isn’t a block frame, so nsBlockFrame::BlockCanIntersectFloats() is
false for it, and it can’t overlap a float either.
